# Commit and Push Discipline

- Maintain small, reviewable commits as work progresses.
- Commit after each meaningful milestone or logical batch of changes.
- Before each commit, run `git status`, review `git diff`, and confirm commit scope.
- Use clear commit messages that state intent and why the change was made.
- Push to the tracked remote branch after successful commits.
- If push is blocked (auth, remote, protection), record the blocker and continue local commits.
- Never use destructive git operations unless explicitly requested.
